  <!--
    The domain the dish is built on (#858). Pure data: `PreparedCookingIngredient` builds its pool
    from every blueprint inheriting `IngredientMapping` - 66 in vanilla - and `Units` resolves
    through `ModManager.ResolveType("XRL.World.Effects." + name)`, which is the XML-names-the-type
    shape charter rule 5 asks for.

    `RandomWeight="0"` keeps it out of vanilla's random cooking table: `GetRandomTypeListInternal`
    runs `while (num > 0)`, so a zero weight is never added. The domain is reachable only through
    dried dunelace - no distribution consequence and no share question.

    `CookingDomain` is set explicitly and must be. With none it falls back to the *mapping
    blueprint's* name via `Split('_')[^1]`, which is what vanilla's `ProceduralCookingIngredient_HP`
    convention is for; a `Vixy_`-prefixed name would resolve to the wrong half.

    One unit, not two. `Units` is `Split(',').GetRandomElement()`, so a second name here would be an
    alternative rather than an addition.
  -->
  <object Name="Vixy_ProceduralCookingIngredient_Rested" Inherits="IngredientMapping">
    <tag Name="CookingDomain" Value="vixyRested" />
    <tag Name="Units" Value="Vixy_CookingDomainRested_UnitStrain" />
    <tag Name="RandomWeight" Value="0" />
  </object>
</objects>
